r['results']=R
I=r['interpretation']
a=I.index("J=1-0 update (team-b p0034")
b=I.index("The S blue-lobe HCN/HCO+ 3-2 excess (1.2-1.4)")
new=("J=1-0 update (team-b p0034, REVISED by p0036/p0034-r02, /snapshots/team-b-s21): adding Band 3 J=1-0 (2.2\" X961 and 1.5\" X145, short-spacing complete; 190-430 pc beams) and re-imaging Band 6 3-2 from visibilities (12m+7m, tapered to the same circular beams) shows that the N/S HCN/HCO+ contrast is the same at J=1-0 and 3-2: 1.47 vs 1.44 at 2.2\" (D=1.00+-0.04; 1.62 vs 1.53 at 1.5\"). The earlier D=1.10+-0.06 and the r31 N>S excess (HCN 1.27, HCO+ 1.13) were artefacts of 12-m flux loss in the Xb4d 3-2 image, which is larger at S (HCN +34% with the 7-m added). With uv-complete data r31 is equal at N and S (N/S 1.01 HCN, 1.03 HCO+, +-0.05) and r31(HCN)~0.26 < r31(HCO+)~0.34: no evidence for an excitation difference between the nuclei, while the lower HCN/HCO+ at the AGN-hosting S nucleus is present at both J. RADEX Bayes factors weakly favour abundance-only over excitation-only (ln BF +1.0 vs +0.2; difference <1, not decisive). ")
I=I[:a]+new+I[b:]
I=I.replace("consistent with the 1-0 persistence and H13CO+ tilt","consistent with the equal N/S contrast at 1-0 and 3-2 (uv-matched) and the H13CO+ tilt")
r['interpretation']=I
r['caveats'][55]=("J=1-0 comparison (p0034/p0036) is at 1.5-2.2\" (190-430 pc) vs 0.95\" native for the 3-2 cubes, so the 50-120 pc N/S 3-2 contrast (2.0-2.1) has no 1-0 counterpart; the Band 6 re-imaging used only 1 of 2 12-m and 3 of 14 7-m EBs, and Band 3 visibilities could not be restored (X961/X145 no manifest; X94a 57.7 GB), so the 1-0 side is matched in beam and short-spacing completeness only, not in identical uv range. Independent 12C/13C and deeper lobe weak-line data are still needed; the S-lobe 1-0 vs 3-2 comparison was not redone with uv-complete 3-2; HCN hyperfines unmodelled and RADEX is one-zone. Earlier 3-2 Xb4d-only ratios/r31 at >=1.5\" apertures carry a 12-m flux-loss bias.")
json.dump(r,open('/output/report.json','w'),indent=1)
